From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: Restore the clip when a first node is rejected

gsk_gpu_node_processor_add_first_node_clipped() saves the node processor's
clip and scissor, narrows them to the candidate first node, and reverts both
when the node turns out not to be usable as the pass's first node. The revert
copied the live clip back over the saved one instead of the other way round:

  gsk_gpu_clip_init_copy (&old_clip, &self->clip);

so self->clip kept the narrowed clip of the rejected candidate while the
scissor was correctly restored. Every later node in that pass was then
processed against a clip that is too small - nodes silently disappear on
partial redraws - and the mismatch between clip and scissor trips the
"Clipping is broken" warning in gsk_gpu_node_processor_sync_globals().

Copy in the other direction so the saved clip is restored.

--- a/gsk/gpu/gskgpunodeprocessor.c
+++ b/gsk/gpu/gskgpunodeprocessor.c
@@ -1435,13 +1435,13 @@
     {
       /* don't revert clip here, the add_first_node() adjusted it to a correct value */
       return TRUE;
     }
 
   self->scissor = old_scissor;
-  gsk_gpu_clip_init_copy (&old_clip, &self->clip);
+  gsk_gpu_clip_init_copy (&self->clip, &old_clip);
 
   return FALSE;
 }
 
 static gboolean
 gsk_gpu_node_processor_add_first_clip_node (GskGpuNodeProcessor *self,
